<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the</p>
<p>third day of rain-affected four-day English County Championship</p>
<p>cricket matches on Friday:</p>
<p>At Chelmsford Essex 246 and 442-8 declared (R.Irani 123 not</p>
<p>out, S.Law 78, P.Prichard 56). Hampshire 161 and 3-0.</p>
<p>At Cardiff: Warwickshire 151 and 77-3. Glamorgan</p>
<p>551-3 declared.</p>
<p>At Canterbury: Kent 251 and 333 (T.Ward 96, P.Strang 69,</p>
<p>M.McCague 53 not out; P.DeFreitas 7-64). Derbyshire 248 and</p>
<p>59-2.</p>
<p>At Old Trafford:  Lancashire 506. Durham 201-6 (D. Boon 85</p>
<p>not out).</p>
<p>At Leicester: Gloucestershire 245 and 8-0. Leicestershire</p>
<p>307.</p>
<p>At Trent Bridge: Worcestershire 417. Nottinghamshire 196-3</p>
<p>(P.Pollard 81, R.Robinson 80).</p>
<p>At The Oval: Somerset 463. Surrey 209-8.</p>
<p>At Hove: Northamptonshire 315. Sussex 411-7 (N. Taylor 127,</p>
<p>K Newell 107not out, P.Jarvis 64).</p>
